WEBVTT

1
00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.967
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:57.474
<i>There's going to be a bus stop</i>
<i>about 300 meters in front of you.</i>

3
00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.975
<i>Do you see it?</i>

4
00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.143
Yes. I see it.

5
00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.936
Crash into the woman

6
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.813
standing there!

7
00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:14.616
Please help my sister.

8
00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:16.493
What do you mean?

9
00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.206
My sister

10
00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:22.916
is Kang Ha-jeong.

11
00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:25.668
Kang Ha-jeong? The accounting manager?

12
00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:30.799
I think…

13
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:34.594
she did something she shouldn't have.

14
00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.679
What do you mean?

15
00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:38.681
She has a ledger.

16
00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:41.976
A ledger recording how
the apartment funds were embezzled.

17
00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:47.106
<i>Kang Ha-jeong. the accounting manager.</i>

18
00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.817
is Kang Ha-ri's sister.

19
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.151
What?

20
00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:54.114
And she has the actual ledger recording
how the reserve fund was embezzled.

21
00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.323
The ledger?

22
00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:56.741
The actual ledger?

23
00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:58.993
Wasn't she working for Lee Chung-won?

24
00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.622
Lee Chung-won
doesn't seem to know about it either.

25
00:02:02.705 --> 00:02:06.251
Ms. Kang probably made it
to protect herself.

26
00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:09.254
Boss. doesn't this mean we have

27
00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.131
-a weapon against him now?
-Right.

28
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.007
Only if we get our hands on it.

29
00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:17.428
You guys keep an eye
on Kang Ha-jeong for now.

30
00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:18.388
-Yes. sir.
-Yes. sir.

31
00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.307
This could be a matter
of life and death for us.

32
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.143
I'm telling you. I can't do this.

33
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:25.812
I'm going to pretend I didn't hear this.

34
00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:47.709
She sat in the third row
from the back of the 125 bus.

35
00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.011
Yes. she's entering her house.

36
00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:03.808
<i>What is it? Did you get caught?</i>

37
00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:04.976
No. it's nothing.

38
00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.854
Ten billion for just driving?

39
00:03:07.937 --> 00:03:10.857
Boss. he's definitely planning
to take someone out.

40
00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.358
You can't do this. Boss.

41
00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:13.860
Boss. I'll do it instead.

42
00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:15.403
I've been the youngest for years.

43
00:03:15.486 --> 00:03:17.405
I have to be a better driver than you.

44
00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:20.241
The "hangnail" Lee Chung-won mentioned
must be Kang Ha-jeong.

45
00:03:23.494 --> 00:03:25.496
Will he stop if I refuse. though?

46
00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:29.042
He'll just get someone
desperate for money to do it instead.

47
00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.336
I need to take the wheel

48
00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:34.005
to get a chance to save Ms. Kang.

49
00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:46.017
Ms. Kang. are you okay?

50
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.060
We're here to help.

51
00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:12.335
This is ten billion won.

52
00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:15.880
I told you I'd give you the money
once you did this.

53
00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:19.008
You can save your old boss
with this money.

54
00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.970
You shouldn't leave him there
when he's already sick.

55
00:04:22.553 --> 00:04:24.555
All you had to do

56
00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:26.683
was crash into a woman
standing right there.

57
00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.726
You've pulled off harder things than that.

58
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.854
but you fail to do the easiest job?

59
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.399
I may be a bad guy.

60
00:04:35.483 --> 00:04:37.193
but you're just trash.

61
00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:39.779
Trash?

62
00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.616
You're being quite rude to a guy
who's interested in you.

63
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.368
I don't date trash.

64
00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.370
Then what will you do with me?

65
00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:50.415
I have an item that will interest you.

66
00:04:50.498 --> 00:04:52.375
A ledger of all the trashy things

67
00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.878
a construction company president did
to embezzle the reserve fund

68
00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.506
of an apartment complex
that he built himself.

69
00:05:05.513 --> 00:05:06.764
Then what about this?

70
00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:10.101
Let's exchange the ledger

71
00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:12.186
for Park Yong-man.

72
00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.981
You needed that ten billion

73
00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:18.151
to get Park Yong-man released.

74
00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.235
So…

75
00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:27.035
COMMISSIONER KWAK JU-GWON

76
00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:34.667
<i>Yes. Mr. Lee.</i>

77
00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.377
<i>What prompts this late-night call?</i>

78
00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:39.881
Commissioner. I have a favor to ask you.

79
00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.507
Let's get ready

80
00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:43.593
to release Park Yong-man on medical bail.

81
00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.721
<i>What? Park Yong-man?</i>

82
00:05:46.804 --> 00:05:49.015
The boss of Park Hae-kang.
the guy you've been using.

83
00:05:49.724 --> 00:05:52.351
I'll let you join the One Club.

84
00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.230
so get ready to release Park Yong-man.

85
00:05:56.898 --> 00:05:58.649
<i>All right. I'll get it ready.</i>

86
00:06:02.737 --> 00:06:04.363
If you want him released.

87
00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:06.991
bring me the ledger.

88
00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:09.410
Simple. isn't it?

89
00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:21.547
My sister really isn't a bad person.

90
00:06:22.256 --> 00:06:23.341
I swear.

91
00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.094
<i>They say it's pancreatic cancer.</i>

92
00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.805
<i>He has about three months left.</i>

93
00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.564
I searched everywhere.
but the ledger isn't here.

94
00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:41.067
It seems she's already moved it.

95
00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.443
<i>It's not there?</i>

96
00:06:43.027 --> 00:06:45.404
Then that means
it's no longer just a document.

97
00:06:46.364 --> 00:06:48.032
It's a weapon now.

98
00:06:48.866 --> 00:06:51.285
I'm sorry. sir. I'll track her again.

99
00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:53.996
She can't hide forever.

100
00:06:55.206 --> 00:06:56.791
Good work. Mr. Kim.

101
00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.463
He really is competent.

102
00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:06.259
But if he keeps being unpredictable.

103
00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.428
it's going to be a problem.

104
00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:13.349
If I turn my back on him…

105
00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:18.146
he won't be able to handle it.

106
00:07:21.023 --> 00:07:25.736
THE APARTMENT JOB

107
00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:40.710
{\an8}Ha-jeong!

108
00:07:42.211 --> 00:07:44.338
{\an8}Ha-jeong. are you okay? Are you hurt?

109
00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:46.591
{\an8}I can't believe this!

110
00:07:46.674 --> 00:07:48.259
{\an8}Tell me.

111
00:07:48.342 --> 00:07:50.344
{\an8}What bastard was trying to kill you?

112
00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:52.763
{\an8}Tell me. You must know who it is!

113
00:07:57.768 --> 00:07:59.979
Who is it? Who did this to my sister?

114
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.357
Where's the ledger?

115
00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:06.027
You almost got killed because of it.

116
00:08:08.112 --> 00:08:09.864
I hid the ledger.

117
00:08:09.947 --> 00:08:11.449
She doesn't know where it is.

118
00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.247
Give me the ledger.

119
00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.583
It's not something you can handle.

120
00:08:22.084 --> 00:08:24.962
And why would you need to take
something that dangerous?

121
00:08:25.755 --> 00:08:26.797
I need it

122
00:08:26.881 --> 00:08:28.633
to at least try to make a deal.

123
00:08:28.716 --> 00:08:29.800
A deal?

124
00:08:30.426 --> 00:08:31.385
With who?

125
00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:33.137
The person who tried to kill my sister?

126
00:08:33.638 --> 00:08:34.472
Who is it?

127
00:08:35.097 --> 00:08:37.016
The former president?
Or the facility manager?

128
00:08:37.099 --> 00:08:38.851
Who is it?

129
00:08:40.895 --> 00:08:43.022
If they want to kill my sister over it.

130
00:08:43.105 --> 00:08:45.107
then that means the ledger
is their weakness.

131
00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:47.735
So why should I hand it over to you?

132
00:08:48.611 --> 00:08:49.570
Mr. Park.

133
00:08:50.446 --> 00:08:52.907
That ledger is also
a record of my sister's crimes.

134
00:08:53.449 --> 00:08:55.034
I can't just hand it over.

135
00:08:55.117 --> 00:08:56.619
The person after her life

136
00:08:57.495 --> 00:08:59.664
isn't someone you can handle.

137
00:08:59.747 --> 00:09:01.916
You're not even telling me
who this person is.

138
00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:03.709
How can I trust you with the ledger?

139
00:09:04.585 --> 00:09:06.295
That ledger is my sister's lifeline.

140
00:09:06.963 --> 00:09:08.881
Her life depends on it right now.

141
00:09:08.965 --> 00:09:09.882
I can't hand it over.

142
00:09:16.347 --> 00:09:17.265
So you mean

143
00:09:17.348 --> 00:09:20.351
the accounting manager
is Kang Ha-ri's sister?

144
00:09:20.935 --> 00:09:23.771
That means she's working
with the penthouse guy.

145
00:09:26.607 --> 00:09:29.318
How did our enemy end up

146
00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:32.029
sitting right in the middle
of our living room?

147
00:09:32.113 --> 00:09:34.615
Hang on. It's going to be tough

148
00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:38.578
having to make meals
for Ms. Kang and her sister too.

149
00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:42.248
There's another mouth to feed now.

150
00:09:42.331 --> 00:09:43.958
Well. this is an emergency.

151
00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:47.295
We just have to set the table
for one more person. right?

152
00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:49.880
Fine. You don't have to be so serious.

153
00:09:51.173 --> 00:09:54.510
I hope she's not a glutton
like somebody here.

154
00:09:59.223 --> 00:10:00.766
Where are you going. Gyeong-buk?

155
00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:03.603
Here.

156
00:10:03.686 --> 00:10:04.854
Kang Ha-ri said

157
00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:07.857
sweets are the best for stress.

158
00:10:11.485 --> 00:10:13.487
CHOCOLATE MILK

159
00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:20.202
Thanks.

160
00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:23.122
So she likes chocolate.

161
00:10:23.664 --> 00:10:24.957
Shameless.

162
00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:27.460
She does seem to like food.

163
00:10:27.543 --> 00:10:31.130
We got the security cam footage
near Kang Ha-jeong's last known location.

164
00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:35.259
She was last seen entering
True Value's Building 114.

165
00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.721
Building 114?
That's where Park Hae-kang lives.

166
00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:39.805
Yes. sir.

167
00:10:40.389 --> 00:10:42.642
We assume she's in his house.

168
00:10:42.725 --> 00:10:44.477
What? Are they dating?

169
00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:47.188
Kang Ha-jeong has a little sister

170
00:10:47.271 --> 00:10:48.689
named Kang Ha-ri.

171
00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:50.816
She's Park Hae-kang's wife.

172
00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:54.028
What's going on here?

173
00:10:54.111 --> 00:10:57.198
So they're in-laws?

174
00:10:57.281 --> 00:10:58.783
It's actually more complicated.

175
00:10:58.866 --> 00:11:02.578
Park Hae-kang and Kang Ha-ri
aren't registered as spouses.

176
00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:05.414
His so-called brothers
are men from his gambling den.

177
00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:07.333
and his father is actually
a wanted gambler.

178
00:11:07.958 --> 00:11:10.711
His entire family is fake.

179
00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:12.672
What?

180
00:11:14.799 --> 00:11:17.218
Wow. You've got to be kidding me.

181
00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:20.221
How ridiculous.

182
00:11:21.097 --> 00:11:22.556
What about his wife?

183
00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:26.310
She was hired through a stand-in service
to play the role of his bride.

184
00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:31.607
So this whole thing was just

185
00:11:32.108 --> 00:11:33.859
a business arrangement between them?

186
00:11:34.443 --> 00:11:36.362
Just a business arrangement.

187
00:11:38.114 --> 00:11:40.116
That means they'll come
wagging their tails

188
00:11:41.617 --> 00:11:43.619
at the smell of money.

189
00:11:44.453 --> 00:11:45.663
How easy.

190
00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.796
I hid the ledger in a safe spot.

191
00:11:55.214 --> 00:11:56.799
No one will be able to find it.

192
00:11:59.927 --> 00:12:00.803
I'm sorry.

193
00:12:01.887 --> 00:12:04.014
I didn't expect things to get this bad.

194
00:12:06.142 --> 00:12:07.059
Who is it?

195
00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:09.478
Who ordered you to embezzle the fund?

196
00:12:10.896 --> 00:12:11.730
It was me.

197
00:12:13.107 --> 00:12:14.525
I made the choice.

198
00:12:15.192 --> 00:12:16.694
Nobody ordered me to do it.

199
00:12:19.321 --> 00:12:20.156
So it's me.

200
00:12:21.574 --> 00:12:22.825
I'm the one who ordered it.

201
00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:25.703
You needed the money to support me.

202
00:12:26.704 --> 00:12:27.538
Ha-ri.

203
00:12:29.331 --> 00:12:30.458
I was so scared

204
00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.002
that something would happen to you.

205
00:12:36.338 --> 00:12:37.173
I'm sorry.

206
00:12:38.007 --> 00:12:39.216
I'm sorry. Ha-ri.

207
00:12:43.179 --> 00:12:46.182
Why won't she give it to you
when things have gotten so bad?

208
00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:49.560
I really didn't expect her to be so cold.

209
00:12:49.643 --> 00:12:50.686
It's understandable.

210
00:12:50.769 --> 00:12:53.397
Her sister's life is on the line.
She won't just hand it over.

211
00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:54.940
Hey. whose side are you on?

212
00:12:55.733 --> 00:12:58.110
Whose side? We're all family here.

213
00:12:58.194 --> 00:12:59.403
Don't be stupid. Boss.

214
00:13:00.237 --> 00:13:01.071
What do we do now?

215
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:02.823
Ms. Kang is right.

216
00:13:03.699 --> 00:13:05.284
Asking her for the ledger

217
00:13:05.367 --> 00:13:07.995
is the same as sacrificing
Kang Ha-jeong for our sake.

218
00:13:08.078 --> 00:13:09.955
Then what about Yong-man?

219
00:13:10.039 --> 00:13:11.707
Without the ledger. how would we--

220
00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.334
That's why we're going with Plan B.

221
00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:15.294
We're going after Lee Chung-won
without the ledger.

222
00:13:15.377 --> 00:13:16.545
Lee Chung-won?

223
00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:21.425
Boss. we'd be fighting against Taesan.

224
00:13:21.509 --> 00:13:23.594
We don't even have
any leverage against them.

225
00:13:23.677 --> 00:13:24.803
I'll make that myself.

226
00:13:25.554 --> 00:13:28.307
But have you guys heard of the One Club?

227
00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.308
One Club?

228
00:13:29.391 --> 00:13:30.559
No. I've never been there.

229
00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:32.228
The one in Hongdae?

230
00:13:34.647 --> 00:13:36.649
<i>I'll let you join the One Club.</i>

231
00:13:37.441 --> 00:13:39.527
so get ready to release Park Yong-man.

232
00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:42.571
The commissioner was behind
Chief Son Dae-un.

233
00:13:43.155 --> 00:13:45.115
The commissioner needed ten billion won

234
00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:46.825
to join this "One Club."

235
00:13:46.909 --> 00:13:48.577
and that's why
Mr. Son demanded it from us.

236
00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:49.620
What?

237
00:13:52.498 --> 00:13:55.501
What kind of big shots
are in this One Club

238
00:13:55.584 --> 00:13:57.127
that you need ten billion to join?

239
00:13:57.753 --> 00:13:58.796
Right?

240
00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:00.422
It seems like

241
00:14:01.257 --> 00:14:03.342
Lee Chung-won is managing that club.

242
00:14:04.301 --> 00:14:06.887
Let's dig into what kind of people
are in this One Club

243
00:14:06.971 --> 00:14:09.932
and what Lee Chung-won is trying

244
00:14:10.015 --> 00:14:11.433
to pull there.

245
00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:12.351
Yes. Boss.

246
00:14:13.269 --> 00:14:14.728
She's not picking up?

247
00:14:15.312 --> 00:14:16.772
No. Her phone's off.

248
00:14:16.855 --> 00:14:19.316
She's not the type to skip work like this.

249
00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:20.651
I wonder what's going on.

250
00:14:22.069 --> 00:14:23.279
Let's focus on work for now.

251
00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:25.030
I'm sure she'll call.

252
00:14:26.156 --> 00:14:27.074
Try calling her again.

253
00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:28.117
-Should I?
-Yes.

254
00:14:30.619 --> 00:14:33.372
<i>Ha-jeong. are you all right?</i>

255
00:14:33.455 --> 00:14:34.290
<i>Say something.</i>

256
00:14:35.082 --> 00:14:36.333
<i>You're scaring me.</i>

257
00:14:37.626 --> 00:14:39.670
Good morning. everyone!

258
00:14:39.753 --> 00:14:40.880
-Hello.
-Good morning.

259
00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:42.756
What brings you here so early?

260
00:14:43.424 --> 00:14:47.303
This is my workplace.
Of course. I should be here.

261
00:14:47.386 --> 00:14:49.138
-Isn't that right?
-Yes. of course.

262
00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:52.266
Mr. Choi.

263
00:14:52.349 --> 00:14:55.769
Please call a meeting
with the tenant representatives.

264
00:14:55.853 --> 00:14:58.355
What? The tenant representatives?

265
00:14:59.273 --> 00:15:01.609
Why do you need…

266
00:15:01.692 --> 00:15:05.487
I'm the president.
I can't sit back and do nothing.

267
00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:08.657
It's my duty to work for this apartment.

268
00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:13.662
Please call a tenants' representative
meeting immediately.

269
00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:21.962
Mom. your eyes are red.

270
00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.007
Did you have a fight with your sister?

271
00:15:25.633 --> 00:15:28.135
No. we just stayed up late chatting.

272
00:15:29.136 --> 00:15:32.264
She looked like
she had a nightmare. though.

273
00:15:34.558 --> 00:15:37.478
I wish Ha-jeong would keep
staying with us.

274
00:15:37.978 --> 00:15:38.979
Why?

275
00:15:39.063 --> 00:15:41.482
Uncle Hae-kang
and my dad will protect her.

276
00:15:42.399 --> 00:15:44.360
Then she won't be scared anymore.

277
00:15:51.033 --> 00:15:52.201
But Mom.

278
00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:57.081
There's a worm
growing in our kindergarten wall.

279
00:15:57.873 --> 00:15:59.917
It keeps getting longer.

280
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.627
I'm scared it'll turn into a snake.

281
00:16:03.128 --> 00:16:04.713
A worm is getting longer?

282
00:16:05.839 --> 00:16:07.925
My teacher told me it's a secret.

283
00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:10.469
So don't tell anyone about it.

284
00:16:18.185 --> 00:16:19.353
-Hello.
-Good morning.

285
00:16:19.436 --> 00:16:21.230
-Hello.
-See you later. Gyeong-buk.

286
00:16:21.313 --> 00:16:22.147
-Okay.
-Bye.

287
00:16:22.231 --> 00:16:23.357
Bye.

288
00:16:26.652 --> 00:16:28.070
-Hello.
-Hello.

289
00:16:28.696 --> 00:16:30.906
Would you like to join us for coffee?

290
00:16:31.699 --> 00:16:32.825
Coffee?

291
00:16:35.911 --> 00:16:38.956
You know Su-a. who transferred
to the Harvard Class yesterday?

292
00:16:39.039 --> 00:16:39.873
I met her mom.

293
00:16:39.957 --> 00:16:42.292
and she said
Su-a got a rash all over her body

294
00:16:42.376 --> 00:16:44.878
as soon as she started
going to kindergarten.

295
00:16:44.962 --> 00:16:46.880
She asked if Seo-jun was okay.

296
00:16:46.964 --> 00:16:51.135
Ru-i actually developed eczema
while attending kindergarten too.

297
00:16:51.218 --> 00:16:54.471
but we couldn't be sure
it was because of that.

298
00:16:54.555 --> 00:16:57.933
You know how we'd suspected
they had used cheap materials?

299
00:16:58.017 --> 00:16:59.643
-Yeah.
-Right.

300
00:16:59.727 --> 00:17:01.061
And Hye-jun told me

301
00:17:01.145 --> 00:17:02.980
she used an umbrella in class yesterday.

302
00:17:03.063 --> 00:17:05.149
so I first thought
they were just having fun.

303
00:17:05.232 --> 00:17:07.067
But she said water fell from the ceiling.

304
00:17:07.151 --> 00:17:08.152
Goodness.

305
00:17:08.235 --> 00:17:10.446
Min-jun said it was raining in class too.

306
00:17:11.155 --> 00:17:13.532
What if it really was shoddy construction?

307
00:17:14.241 --> 00:17:16.660
There's a worm
growing in our kindergarten wall.

308
00:17:17.244 --> 00:17:18.912
It keeps getting longer.

309
00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:21.707
We filed a complaint
with the Office of Education.

310
00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.500
-but they said it's fine.
-Right.

311
00:17:23.584 --> 00:17:25.919
A private inspection company came
and checked everything.

312
00:17:26.003 --> 00:17:26.837
They said it's safe.

313
00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.506
Well. it's the law.
What else can we do anyway?

314
00:17:30.132 --> 00:17:31.717
It's not the law.

315
00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.135
The method was wrong.

316
00:17:33.886 --> 00:17:37.056
Don't trust the kindergarten.
File an information disclosure request.

317
00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:39.516
We should compare each item
on the diagnostic report.

318
00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.268
We can view the report?

319
00:17:41.977 --> 00:17:43.062
It's our right as citizens.

320
00:17:43.771 --> 00:17:46.065
This should be reported
as a public interest violation.

321
00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:49.276
Children's safety
is a matter of public interest.

322
00:17:49.359 --> 00:17:50.360
If we report this

323
00:17:50.444 --> 00:17:52.946
to the Civil Rights Commission.
the officials will have to act.

324
00:17:54.448 --> 00:17:56.909
You're so smart. Ms. Kang.

325
00:17:56.992 --> 00:17:59.244
How do you know stuff like that?

326
00:18:00.287 --> 00:18:02.498
I just know a tiny bit.

327
00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:07.294
Then you can come with us
to the Office of Education.

328
00:18:07.878 --> 00:18:08.712
She's right.

329
00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:09.922
-That's a great idea.
-Yes.

330
00:18:10.547 --> 00:18:11.381
Me?

331
00:18:11.465 --> 00:18:13.258
-Let's go together.
-Right.

332
00:18:13.342 --> 00:18:14.843
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

333
00:18:15.427 --> 00:18:16.720
I'm so glad.

334
00:18:18.764 --> 00:18:21.350
Why did I have to say that?

335
00:18:21.433 --> 00:18:22.851
I'm not even a lawyer.

336
00:18:23.352 --> 00:18:25.729
You should stop meddling
in other people's lives.

337
00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:28.107
Just worry about yourself and Ha-jeong.

338
00:18:30.192 --> 00:18:32.236
President Park's wife?

339
00:18:37.074 --> 00:18:38.617
Yes. that's me.

340
00:18:39.451 --> 00:18:40.285
Who…

341
00:18:43.997 --> 00:18:48.210
I'm just curious how much you know
about your husband.

342
00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.424
Should I call you Kang Ha-jeong's sister?

343
00:18:59.096 --> 00:19:01.056
{\an8}UNDER REPAIR
WILL BE COMPLETED SOON

344
00:19:02.057 --> 00:19:03.725
Here. Kang Ha-ri.

345
00:19:06.186 --> 00:19:09.064
Your sister did something quite bold.

346
00:19:11.483 --> 00:19:12.776
So it's you.

347
00:19:13.861 --> 00:19:15.362
You tried to kill my sister.

348
00:19:15.946 --> 00:19:17.406
You're quick-witted.

349
00:19:17.489 --> 00:19:19.366
You're right. That was me.

350
00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:22.035
You bastard.

351
00:19:22.703 --> 00:19:25.914
You're smart. but you're naive.

352
00:19:27.249 --> 00:19:29.001
Am I the only bad guy here?

353
00:19:29.084 --> 00:19:31.336
Is your sister a good person. then?

354
00:19:32.421 --> 00:19:34.256
Your sister teamed up with a bad guy

355
00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:37.801
and helped him cover up his crimes.

356
00:19:42.598 --> 00:19:44.600
How about 500 million?

357
00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:47.644
Your sister's severance pay and bonus.

358
00:19:47.728 --> 00:19:50.397
But I want that ledger in return.

359
00:19:54.067 --> 00:19:55.194
Why not?

360
00:19:55.277 --> 00:19:58.864
I'm sure that's more than what you got
for playing Park Hae-kang's wife.

361
00:20:07.289 --> 00:20:09.458
The pay is better.
but the benefits aren't that great.

362
00:20:10.751 --> 00:20:12.920
How can I trust a boss
who tried to kill someone

363
00:20:13.003 --> 00:20:14.463
who worked for him?

364
00:20:15.839 --> 00:20:17.424
So you're the type to hold grudges.

365
00:20:17.507 --> 00:20:18.926
Forget it.

366
00:20:21.011 --> 00:20:22.512
If you touch my sister again.

367
00:20:23.972 --> 00:20:26.433
I'll make you realize you messed

368
00:20:26.516 --> 00:20:28.143
with the wrong person.

369
00:20:28.852 --> 00:20:30.854
Your sister is staying
at Park Hae-kang's. right?

370
00:20:31.563 --> 00:20:35.525
Do you really think Park Hae-kang
will protect you two until the end?

371
00:20:37.486 --> 00:20:39.780
At least he doesn't
stab people in the back.

372
00:20:42.115 --> 00:20:44.159
You really have no clue. do you?

373
00:20:46.203 --> 00:20:48.914
Park Hae-kang actually came here

374
00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:52.876
to take the 17 billion won
in the reserve fund.

375
00:20:56.088 --> 00:20:58.840
He can only take the fund
if he's the president.

376
00:20:59.508 --> 00:21:01.635
He's been using you.

377
00:21:02.844 --> 00:21:04.137
Do you still not get it?

378
00:21:09.768 --> 00:21:11.061
Gyeong-buk.

379
00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:14.064
Hang on.

380
00:21:17.609 --> 00:21:18.777
Candied sweet potatoes.

381
00:21:21.571 --> 00:21:22.489
Are you dreaming?

382
00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:23.991
Move.

383
00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:26.785
You were right.

384
00:21:28.704 --> 00:21:30.747
I was bored just sitting around.

385
00:21:30.831 --> 00:21:33.792
There were some sweet potatoes.
so I made a snack for Gyeong-buk.

386
00:21:33.875 --> 00:21:35.585
I made plenty. so have some.

387
00:21:36.461 --> 00:21:38.005
I didn't know you had such talent.

388
00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.843
Come and have some. They're tasty.

389
00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:03.113
Your gaze

390
00:22:03.196 --> 00:22:05.866
is sweeter
than the candied sweet potatoes.

391
00:22:09.077 --> 00:22:10.495
Come and try this.

392
00:22:10.579 --> 00:22:12.039
-Come on.
-Come here.

393
00:22:12.122 --> 00:22:13.040
Try some.

394
00:22:14.875 --> 00:22:16.126
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

395
00:22:16.209 --> 00:22:17.377
You're welcome.

396
00:22:19.963 --> 00:22:20.839
Mr. Park.

397
00:22:22.883 --> 00:22:24.009
Where's Park Hae-kang?

398
00:22:24.593 --> 00:22:25.761
Come out here!

399
00:22:25.844 --> 00:22:27.637
Ha-ri. what's wrong?

400
00:22:30.891 --> 00:22:31.892
What?

401
00:22:33.101 --> 00:22:35.437
-What is it?
-Is it true?

402
00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:36.354
Is what true?

403
00:22:37.022 --> 00:22:39.399
The reason why you were
desperate to become the president.

404
00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:42.986
Was it all

405
00:22:44.362 --> 00:22:46.239
because of the 17 billion
in the reserve fund?

406
00:22:57.375 --> 00:22:58.877
Did you meet Lee Chung-won?

407
00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:02.172
Yes.

408
00:23:02.255 --> 00:23:04.299
I could tell when I met him.

409
00:23:05.717 --> 00:23:07.594
That man is openly evil.

410
00:23:07.677 --> 00:23:10.055
but you're a real fraud
who pretends to be a good guy

411
00:23:10.138 --> 00:23:11.973
-while stabbing people in the back.
-Ms. Kang.

412
00:23:12.057 --> 00:23:13.683
You're being too harsh…

413
00:23:18.438 --> 00:23:19.815
So?

414
00:23:21.775 --> 00:23:24.528
Do you feel betrayed because I'm a fraud?

415
00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:26.655
Ms. Kang.

416
00:23:27.531 --> 00:23:29.491
stop pretending like you're a victim.

417
00:23:31.993 --> 00:23:32.828
What?

418
00:23:32.911 --> 00:23:35.372
You pretended to be my wife
because you needed money too.

419
00:23:35.455 --> 00:23:36.706
Method acting?

420
00:23:37.457 --> 00:23:38.416
Paid labor?

421
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.085
Don't be silly.

422
00:23:40.168 --> 00:23:44.131
You chose to be part of a fake family
because of money.

423
00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:50.720
You're right.

424
00:23:51.304 --> 00:23:52.681
I did this for the money.

425
00:23:52.764 --> 00:23:54.474
But at the very least.

426
00:23:55.308 --> 00:23:58.687
I never betrayed people's trust
while pretending to be righteous.

427
00:23:59.396 --> 00:24:02.274
I thought you were sincerely
trying to make this a better place.

428
00:24:03.066 --> 00:24:04.067
I just feel

429
00:24:05.193 --> 00:24:08.530
so embarrassed
that I took your side because of that.

430
00:24:11.741 --> 00:24:12.576
Ha-jeong.

431
00:24:13.577 --> 00:24:15.495
Let's go. I can't stay here any longer.

432
00:24:17.998 --> 00:24:19.291
What will you do once you leave?

433
00:24:21.668 --> 00:24:23.420
Why do you think
Lee Chung-won met with you?

434
00:24:25.297 --> 00:24:26.173
This means

435
00:24:26.840 --> 00:24:28.300
he knows where Ha-jeong is.

436
00:24:30.177 --> 00:24:32.679
Let's talk inside for a moment.

437
00:24:46.568 --> 00:24:47.652
Park Hae-kang

438
00:24:48.862 --> 00:24:51.072
saved me when I almost died.

439
00:24:52.032 --> 00:24:53.700
I know that.

440
00:24:53.783 --> 00:24:56.369
but he's also the one
who planned all this to take the fund.

441
00:24:57.037 --> 00:25:00.624
You did this because of money too.
Why do you expect him to be innocent?

442
00:25:06.421 --> 00:25:10.175
He saved me when he knew
that 17 billion was already gone.

443
00:25:11.301 --> 00:25:14.471
You keeping the ledger hidden
isn't helping him in any way.

444
00:25:14.554 --> 00:25:15.972
but look.

445
00:25:16.056 --> 00:25:18.934
He's putting himself at risk
by protecting us.

446
00:25:23.813 --> 00:25:25.023
You may be used to

447
00:25:26.441 --> 00:25:31.321
being called a fraud and a thug
by other people.

448
00:25:31.404 --> 00:25:34.783
but it must be the first time
hearing it from someone who trusted you.

449
00:25:36.868 --> 00:25:39.329
That's why you have
that look on your face.

450
00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:41.915
What look?

451
00:25:44.542 --> 00:25:46.419
You look like you got caught being human

452
00:25:47.003 --> 00:25:49.214
despite being a fraud.

453
00:25:54.177 --> 00:25:56.471
Let's begin True Value State's first

454
00:25:56.554 --> 00:25:59.391
tenants' representative council meeting.

455
00:26:00.642 --> 00:26:03.937
Welcome. everyone.

456
00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:09.484
We did name this
a tenants' council meeting.

457
00:26:09.567 --> 00:26:10.944
but our real goal

458
00:26:11.027 --> 00:26:13.405
is for everyone to get along here.

459
00:26:13.488 --> 00:26:17.242
regardless of whether
the unit is a rental or owner-occupied.

460
00:26:18.368 --> 00:26:21.746
Everything you say is absolutely right.

461
00:26:23.331 --> 00:26:25.583
Do you have any ideas. President Jang?

462
00:26:25.667 --> 00:26:26.501
I would like

463
00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:31.047
to suggest a safety patrol.

464
00:26:31.673 --> 00:26:35.510
But President Jang.
we already have guards…

465
00:26:37.304 --> 00:26:41.516
Before arguing about
who the true owners of True Value are.

466
00:26:41.599 --> 00:26:43.435
we should show everyone

467
00:26:43.518 --> 00:26:46.438
that we're the ones

468
00:26:46.521 --> 00:26:50.066
who care the most about this place.

469
00:26:50.817 --> 00:26:51.985
So.

470
00:26:52.068 --> 00:26:53.695
starting tonight.

471
00:26:53.778 --> 00:26:56.614
who wants to join me
in patrolling the complex?

472
00:27:02.078 --> 00:27:03.747
Right. Thank you.

473
00:27:05.123 --> 00:27:06.750
I knew it.

474
00:27:08.418 --> 00:27:10.837
We elected such good representatives.

475
00:27:11.504 --> 00:27:13.798
Cats never come this way.

476
00:27:13.882 --> 00:27:15.133
They always stay over there.

477
00:27:16.176 --> 00:27:17.635
Gosh. Look.

478
00:27:18.303 --> 00:27:19.304
The light's off.

479
00:27:19.387 --> 00:27:21.389
The trail in front of Building 107.

480
00:27:21.473 --> 00:27:22.766
-Write that down.
-Okay.

481
00:27:22.849 --> 00:27:23.850
Okay.

482
00:27:23.933 --> 00:27:25.393
Shall we go that way?

483
00:27:26.227 --> 00:27:27.187
Excuse me.

484
00:27:28.146 --> 00:27:30.148
-Where do you live?
-Building 109.

485
00:27:30.231 --> 00:27:31.483
This building?

486
00:27:31.566 --> 00:27:33.443
We're True Value's safety patrol.

487
00:27:33.526 --> 00:27:36.363
The building reps are working hard
for this apartment complex.

488
00:27:37.530 --> 00:27:39.157
-This building?
-Yes.

489
00:27:39.240 --> 00:27:41.618
-You shouldn't stay out too late.
-Okay.

490
00:27:41.701 --> 00:27:43.161
-It's a dangerous world.
-Right.

491
00:27:43.244 --> 00:27:44.204
You can't see me.

492
00:27:44.287 --> 00:27:45.580
No. you hold it.

493
00:27:46.706 --> 00:27:48.458
Stretch your arm out. okay?

494
00:27:49.292 --> 00:27:50.293
Kids!

495
00:27:51.461 --> 00:27:53.213
What are you doing?

496
00:27:53.296 --> 00:27:55.799
It's late. you know.

497
00:27:56.841 --> 00:27:58.843
Hyeong-u. don't you live in Building 105?

498
00:27:58.927 --> 00:28:00.720
Yes. Hello.

499
00:28:00.804 --> 00:28:02.680
Your mom will be waiting. Go home.

500
00:28:02.764 --> 00:28:04.599
How many girlfriends do you have?

501
00:28:04.682 --> 00:28:05.767
Gosh!

502
00:28:06.309 --> 00:28:07.143
I'll call you!

503
00:28:07.227 --> 00:28:08.353
-Don't.
-Okay.

504
00:28:08.436 --> 00:28:09.938
Stop making your mom worry!

505
00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:12.399
Everyone knows
he gives his mom a hard time.

506
00:28:12.482 --> 00:28:13.983
He's too handsome for his own good.

507
00:28:14.567 --> 00:28:16.486
Great work today. everyone.

508
00:28:16.569 --> 00:28:18.238
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

509
00:28:18.321 --> 00:28:19.781
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-All right.

510
00:28:19.864 --> 00:28:21.991
I'm going to take a detour back home.

511
00:28:22.075 --> 00:28:23.743
-Okay.
-Bye.

512
00:28:23.827 --> 00:28:25.286
-Bye.
-Bye.

513
00:28:25.370 --> 00:28:26.704
-Bye.
-Bye.

514
00:28:26.788 --> 00:28:29.416
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

515
00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:41.010
What is that?

516
00:28:52.355 --> 00:28:53.606
What is all this?

517
00:28:54.232 --> 00:28:55.191
Goodness.

518
00:28:55.692 --> 00:28:57.068
It's going to crumble down soon.

519
00:28:57.736 --> 00:28:59.028
My gosh.

520
00:29:07.579 --> 00:29:08.455
You scared me.

521
00:29:09.164 --> 00:29:11.207
What are you doing?

522
00:29:16.713 --> 00:29:18.590
Why do I feel so thirsty?

523
00:29:22.469 --> 00:29:23.428
Do you remember

524
00:29:24.012 --> 00:29:27.599
how you said it feels
like you have to repay your sister?

525
00:29:30.185 --> 00:29:31.478
What about it?

526
00:29:32.145 --> 00:29:33.772
I told you I have someone like that too.

527
00:29:35.190 --> 00:29:36.024
So?

528
00:29:37.567 --> 00:29:38.443
That person

529
00:29:39.402 --> 00:29:40.987
is in jail right now.

530
00:29:41.946 --> 00:29:43.072
And he's innocent.

531
00:29:43.573 --> 00:29:47.118
For people like me.
there are only two ways

532
00:29:47.202 --> 00:29:48.953
to get involved with the police.

533
00:29:49.954 --> 00:29:51.790
Greasing their palms
and coexisting with them.

534
00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:54.334
or getting hauled in as a suspect.

535
00:29:58.296 --> 00:29:59.714
I did the former.

536
00:30:00.507 --> 00:30:03.259
I was one of their favorite cash cows.

537
00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:08.056
But the ones who thought of me
as a goose laying golden eggs

538
00:30:08.139 --> 00:30:11.267
took my old boss to cut me open.

539
00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:13.895
And they told me to bring ten billion

540
00:30:15.313 --> 00:30:16.898
if I wanted to get him released.

541
00:30:18.733 --> 00:30:23.154
That's when I found out
there was money in this apartment complex.

542
00:30:24.364 --> 00:30:26.783
I did all this
because of the reserve fund.

543
00:30:27.367 --> 00:30:29.828
It's true I became the president
with ill intentions.

544
00:30:29.911 --> 00:30:33.164
And it's true that I dragged you into this

545
00:30:33.248 --> 00:30:34.999
when you had no clue.

546
00:30:37.085 --> 00:30:39.754
I just thought it would be better
for you not to know.

547
00:30:40.797 --> 00:30:41.673
but I guess

548
00:30:43.299 --> 00:30:44.551
I've only deceived you.

549
00:30:48.555 --> 00:30:49.556
I apologize.

550
00:30:51.683 --> 00:30:52.684
I'm sorry.

551
00:30:58.189 --> 00:30:59.440
So what will you do now?

552
00:31:00.692 --> 00:31:04.112
There's no money in the account.
and I won't give you the ledger.

553
00:31:05.446 --> 00:31:07.156
I'll find another way.

554
00:31:08.241 --> 00:31:09.325
Even so.

555
00:31:10.159 --> 00:31:13.454
I promise to keep the two of you safe.

556
00:31:19.294 --> 00:31:21.004
I promise.

557
00:31:25.341 --> 00:31:27.427
Have it with a poached egg.

558
00:31:27.510 --> 00:31:28.636
This isn't cheese?

559
00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:29.762
All right.

560
00:31:31.306 --> 00:31:33.600
Here. Enjoy.

561
00:31:34.183 --> 00:31:35.727
Asparagus?

562
00:31:38.813 --> 00:31:39.647
Gyeong-buk.

563
00:31:40.315 --> 00:31:42.358
Tell Ha-ri to eat.

564
00:31:43.109 --> 00:31:46.112
Ha-ri. Uncle Hae-kang said you should eat.

565
00:31:46.779 --> 00:31:50.074
Gyeong-buk. tell your uncle
that I don't have an appetite.

566
00:31:51.993 --> 00:31:53.703
She doesn't have an appetite?

567
00:31:53.786 --> 00:31:56.581
She'll have no energy all day
if she skips breakfast.

568
00:31:56.664 --> 00:31:58.541
Tell her to at least have a bite.

569
00:32:00.084 --> 00:32:01.711
Tell him to stay out of my business

570
00:32:01.794 --> 00:32:04.255
and enjoy his own meal.

571
00:32:08.551 --> 00:32:10.053
My teacher said

572
00:32:10.136 --> 00:32:12.055
fighting is bad.

573
00:32:12.138 --> 00:32:15.099
and not making up after that
is even worse.

574
00:32:15.183 --> 00:32:16.434
You're awful.

575
00:32:17.393 --> 00:32:19.187
Gyeong-buk. we're not fighting--

576
00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:20.146
Just make up.

577
00:32:20.897 --> 00:32:23.524
If you don't.
I'm not going to kindergarten today.

578
00:32:23.608 --> 00:32:24.567
I'm not eating. either!

579
00:32:25.401 --> 00:32:27.612
-Good job. Gyeong-buk!
-Nice!

580
00:32:27.695 --> 00:32:28.655
Gyeong-buk's angry.

581
00:32:28.738 --> 00:32:30.114
Fine. let's make up.

582
00:32:30.198 --> 00:32:31.699
Okay. Let's make up.

583
00:32:31.783 --> 00:32:33.910
Gyeong-buk. we made up.

584
00:32:33.993 --> 00:32:35.870
-We made up.
-We made up.

585
00:32:35.954 --> 00:32:37.038
Now hug each other.

586
00:32:37.538 --> 00:32:38.957
-What?
-What?

587
00:32:39.040 --> 00:32:42.293
My teacher said you have to hug
when you apologize.

588
00:32:42.377 --> 00:32:45.004
No. there's no need.

589
00:32:45.964 --> 00:32:48.466
Gyeong-buk's teacher is very wise.

590
00:32:49.717 --> 00:32:52.512
Come on. We should apologize too.

591
00:32:52.595 --> 00:32:53.596
Let's make up.

592
00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:55.098
-We should apologize.
-What?

593
00:32:55.181 --> 00:32:56.224
-What…
-Let's make up.

594
00:32:56.307 --> 00:32:57.517
No. it's fine.

595
00:32:57.600 --> 00:32:58.726
Let's go.

596
00:32:58.810 --> 00:33:00.436
-I said it's fine!
-They need to hug?

597
00:33:00.520 --> 00:33:01.896
What are you doing?

598
00:33:02.772 --> 00:33:04.607
Okay. fine. Let's make up.

599
00:33:04.691 --> 00:33:06.192
We're making up.

600
00:33:06.275 --> 00:33:07.568
-Let's make up.
-Bigger hug!

601
00:33:08.236 --> 00:33:09.487
-Bigger hug!
-Bigger hug!

602
00:33:16.035 --> 00:33:18.830
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN
ENROLLMENT OPEN

603
00:33:23.459 --> 00:33:25.378
What do I do?

604
00:33:27.922 --> 00:33:29.090
If I expose this.

605
00:33:29.173 --> 00:33:31.300
I'll become a traitor to True Value.

606
00:33:33.136 --> 00:33:35.054
Bye!

607
00:33:36.431 --> 00:33:37.598
Mom!

608
00:33:42.854 --> 00:33:45.273
Gosh. This is giving me a headache.

609
00:33:45.356 --> 00:33:46.691
Oh dear.

610
00:33:50.862 --> 00:33:54.198
Construction will officially start
next month.

611
00:33:55.283 --> 00:33:56.659
I wanted you to see the empty plot

612
00:33:58.036 --> 00:33:59.579
before that.

613
00:33:59.662 --> 00:34:02.331
Everything here will change completely.

614
00:34:02.415 --> 00:34:04.667
You should see this place one last time.

615
00:34:05.418 --> 00:34:08.421
I hope you'll care about the project
as it takes shape

616
00:34:08.504 --> 00:34:11.382
and show lots of support.

617
00:34:11.466 --> 00:34:13.926
You know my son-in-law's
law firm represents

618
00:34:15.219 --> 00:34:17.096
the top legal figures in Korea. right?

619
00:34:17.180 --> 00:34:18.014
Yes.

620
00:34:18.097 --> 00:34:21.392
So proceed with the project
without worrying about legal issues.

621
00:34:21.476 --> 00:34:23.102
Speed is the most important.

622
00:34:23.186 --> 00:34:26.481
The relic incident slowed things down.
Let's speed things up.

623
00:34:26.564 --> 00:34:29.776
Of course. I'll have everything
moving so fast. it'll be hard to keep up.

624
00:34:29.859 --> 00:34:31.527
We're going to start releasing articles.

625
00:34:31.611 --> 00:34:33.529
I'll get the prices up.

626
00:34:34.238 --> 00:34:36.449
The VIP is keeping an eye on this as well.

627
00:34:37.200 --> 00:34:39.952
Oman New Town is emerging
as a potential solution

628
00:34:40.661 --> 00:34:44.415
to the housing shortage in Seoul!

629
00:34:46.834 --> 00:34:48.753
We'll provide
all the policy support you need.

630
00:34:48.836 --> 00:34:49.921
Thank you.

631
00:34:51.047 --> 00:34:52.298
Thank you. everyone!

632
00:34:54.175 --> 00:34:55.510
{\an8}OMAN NEW TOWN
GEOLOGICAL SURVEY

633
00:34:55.593 --> 00:34:57.386
{\an8}Let's zoom in.

634
00:34:58.054 --> 00:34:59.931
I can even see their pores.

635
00:35:00.014 --> 00:35:01.641
This camera is amazing.

636
00:35:01.724 --> 00:35:03.226
Can you tell who they are?

637
00:35:05.645 --> 00:35:06.521
That guy…

638
00:35:07.146 --> 00:35:09.023
I saw him on the news.

639
00:35:09.107 --> 00:35:11.984
Who was he again?
He's always with the president.

640
00:35:12.068 --> 00:35:13.861
The Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.

641
00:35:13.945 --> 00:35:15.780
And the president of <i>Gongyeong Daily.</i>

642
00:35:15.863 --> 00:35:18.074
They're all gathered
to fill their pockets.

643
00:35:18.157 --> 00:35:20.076
My fingers are trembling.

644
00:35:20.159 --> 00:35:21.869
Get their faces clearly.

645
00:35:23.079 --> 00:35:25.331
These will be their memorial photos.

646
00:35:32.630 --> 00:35:34.215
You're not allowed to take photos here.

647
00:35:34.298 --> 00:35:36.676
-Sorry about that.
-Move your equipment.

648
00:35:37.635 --> 00:35:40.054
We had to conduct a geological survey.

649
00:35:40.138 --> 00:35:43.349
We're just here to do our job. Look!

650
00:35:43.432 --> 00:35:44.392
We're heading out.

651
00:35:44.475 --> 00:35:45.810
We'll wrap up now!

652
00:35:45.893 --> 00:35:47.353
We're almost done.

653
00:35:47.436 --> 00:35:49.313
ONE CLUB

654
00:35:49.397 --> 00:35:50.565
Look. Boss.

655
00:35:51.149 --> 00:35:53.317
Construction. law.

656
00:35:53.401 --> 00:35:54.569
politics.

657
00:35:55.194 --> 00:35:56.279
media.

658
00:35:56.362 --> 00:35:58.531
Korea's most powerful figures
are all gathered here.

659
00:36:01.284 --> 00:36:03.035
Can you recognize this man?

660
00:36:03.870 --> 00:36:05.538
The Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.

661
00:36:05.621 --> 00:36:07.623
The official right below the president.

662
00:36:07.707 --> 00:36:10.293
And next to him
is the Supreme Court Justice.

663
00:36:10.376 --> 00:36:11.544
And in the back

664
00:36:11.627 --> 00:36:15.006
are the president of <i>Gongyeong Daily</i>
and the Prosecutor General.

665
00:36:16.299 --> 00:36:18.676
They're the members of the One Club.

666
00:36:19.427 --> 00:36:21.512
No wonder he wasn't scared of anything.

667
00:36:21.596 --> 00:36:24.265
He was using
the entire country as his shield.

668
00:36:29.562 --> 00:36:30.980
I didn't order any food.

669
00:36:31.898 --> 00:36:33.149
Ms. Kang.

670
00:36:34.692 --> 00:36:37.236
What is it? I was sleeping…

671
00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:40.198
Look at this.

672
00:36:44.243 --> 00:36:45.661
What is this?

673
00:36:45.745 --> 00:36:48.206
That's Gyeong-buk's kindergarten.

674
00:36:49.373 --> 00:36:53.044
That's what the exterior wall
looks like right now.

675
00:36:53.127 --> 00:36:54.837
But we can see the rebar.

676
00:36:54.921 --> 00:36:57.381
Couldn't the building
collapse at any moment?

677
00:36:57.465 --> 00:37:00.551
The kindergarten mothers
suspected shoddy construction too.

678
00:37:00.635 --> 00:37:04.472
I've been so torn about what to do.

679
00:37:04.555 --> 00:37:07.099
If I expose this issue.

680
00:37:07.183 --> 00:37:09.185
the apartment prices will drop for sure.

681
00:37:09.268 --> 00:37:12.271
and they'll attack the rental units again.

682
00:37:12.355 --> 00:37:14.357
saying we don't care if the prices drop.

683
00:37:15.441 --> 00:37:17.777
Still. this isn't a trivial matter.

684
00:37:20.988 --> 00:37:21.822
President Park.

685
00:37:22.740 --> 00:37:25.409
I think you should step up
and handle this.

686
00:37:27.995 --> 00:37:28.871
All right.

687
00:37:29.413 --> 00:37:31.666
This involves the safety of the kids here.

688
00:37:31.749 --> 00:37:33.542
Of course.
I should step up as the president.

689
00:37:35.711 --> 00:37:37.338
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

690
00:37:41.968 --> 00:37:43.177
Wait just a moment.

691
00:37:45.429 --> 00:37:46.973
Are you filming a prison escape movie?

692
00:37:47.056 --> 00:37:49.183
<i>Papillon</i> really ruined all you kids.

693
00:37:54.480 --> 00:37:56.023
Are you filming a spy movie or what?

694
00:37:56.107 --> 00:37:58.234
Tom Cruise really ruined all you kids.

695
00:37:59.026 --> 00:37:59.986
This isn't mine.

696
00:38:00.069 --> 00:38:01.279
That's mine.

697
00:38:01.362 --> 00:38:02.613
Everyone. move aside.

698
00:38:03.114 --> 00:38:04.323
Let me smash it in.

699
00:38:07.827 --> 00:38:08.744
Get a grip!

700
00:38:08.828 --> 00:38:12.248
It'll cost the residents money
to get it fixed if you break it.

701
00:38:13.082 --> 00:38:15.084
Ma Dong-seok ruined all you kids.

702
00:38:15.167 --> 00:38:16.043
Step back!

703
00:38:17.878 --> 00:38:18.838
Move aside.

704
00:38:25.094 --> 00:38:27.388
<i>Security has been disabled.</i>

705
00:38:28.723 --> 00:38:30.182
You had a key?

706
00:38:30.266 --> 00:38:33.102
-You should've told us.
-I told you.

707
00:38:33.853 --> 00:38:35.604
He's got main character syndrome.

708
00:38:40.818 --> 00:38:42.445
All right. Gosh.

709
00:38:45.906 --> 00:38:47.408
Check thoroughly.

710
00:38:49.785 --> 00:38:53.122
Cracks in the wall and stuff.

711
00:38:53.205 --> 00:38:54.957
Check if there's anything off.

712
00:38:55.833 --> 00:38:57.293
We'll check thoroughly.

713
00:39:06.635 --> 00:39:09.013
You idiot. Are you stealing kids' candy?

714
00:39:09.096 --> 00:39:10.931
Are you here to stuff your face?

715
00:39:51.806 --> 00:39:53.182
Worm.

716
00:39:53.265 --> 00:39:55.059
Right. The worm.

717
00:40:00.314 --> 00:40:01.440
What's that?

718
00:40:12.243 --> 00:40:14.578
Are you crying?

719
00:40:16.163 --> 00:40:17.665
No…

720
00:40:22.253 --> 00:40:23.546
It's leaking.

721
00:40:35.850 --> 00:40:37.143
Oh my gosh.

722
00:40:37.935 --> 00:40:40.062
It wasn't just one crack.

723
00:40:43.566 --> 00:40:45.693
Is this the spot you were talking about?

724
00:40:45.776 --> 00:40:46.777
Pull it back.

725
00:40:49.864 --> 00:40:51.532
You shouldn't see this. Mr. Kim.

726
00:40:51.615 --> 00:40:52.867
-Why?
-Hey.

727
00:40:52.950 --> 00:40:54.827
-Stay calm.
-Let go.

728
00:40:58.914 --> 00:41:00.124
What is this?

729
00:41:01.917 --> 00:41:04.837
The mothers filed a complaint.
so an inspection company came.

730
00:41:04.920 --> 00:41:05.963
but they said it was safe.

731
00:41:06.547 --> 00:41:08.215
What part of this is safe?

732
00:41:08.299 --> 00:41:09.800
This is practically attempted murder.

733
00:41:09.884 --> 00:41:12.052
I can't believe these assholes.

734
00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:14.054
I guess Taesan really is powerful.

735
00:41:14.138 --> 00:41:16.348
How could they even
think about covering this up?

736
00:41:16.432 --> 00:41:18.893
That's why we need to figure out
what to do about this.

737
00:41:20.102 --> 00:41:21.479
What should we do. President Park?

738
00:41:28.944 --> 00:41:30.279
No. Never.

739
00:41:30.362 --> 00:41:32.448
You can't go to kindergarten today.

740
00:41:33.032 --> 00:41:33.866
Why not?

741
00:41:35.201 --> 00:41:37.661
Well. the kindergarten…

742
00:41:37.745 --> 00:41:38.829
-Just don't go.
-I…

743
00:41:38.913 --> 00:41:42.124
I also want you
to skip kindergarten today.

744
00:41:43.626 --> 00:41:45.544
Then who will I play with?

745
00:41:46.837 --> 00:41:48.964
We can all play with you.

746
00:41:50.424 --> 00:41:51.675
Why are you looking at me?

747
00:42:00.684 --> 00:42:03.604
Do you not care about the other kids?

748
00:42:03.687 --> 00:42:05.564
It's fine as long as your kid is safe?

749
00:42:06.148 --> 00:42:09.443
Turning a blind eye
makes you equally guilty. Mr. Park.

750
00:42:12.238 --> 00:42:13.989
All right. I'll let you

751
00:42:14.073 --> 00:42:15.824
play at a kids cafe today.

752
00:42:15.908 --> 00:42:17.451
And bring all your friends!

753
00:42:20.037 --> 00:42:21.664
You're the best!

754
00:42:22.289 --> 00:42:23.916
Why is he so excited?

755
00:42:24.708 --> 00:42:26.085
What's a kids cafe?

756
00:42:27.253 --> 00:42:29.838
It's like an indoor playground for kids

757
00:42:29.922 --> 00:42:31.966
and a battleground for parents.

758
00:42:57.241 --> 00:42:58.367
Wait!

759
00:42:58.450 --> 00:43:00.160
I'm afraid of heights.

760
00:43:13.299 --> 00:43:14.216
Why isn't it falling?

761
00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.718
Call the manager!

762
00:43:15.801 --> 00:43:17.469
Why do you need the manager?

763
00:43:23.934 --> 00:43:25.019
I got it!

764
00:43:25.102 --> 00:43:25.936
Good job!

765
00:43:26.020 --> 00:43:28.522
Bathroom! Where's the bathroom?

766
00:43:39.533 --> 00:43:40.367
I'm so exhausted.

767
00:43:40.451 --> 00:43:41.952
How are they so full of energy?

768
00:43:42.036 --> 00:43:43.954
Delivering packages was easier than this.

769
00:43:45.998 --> 00:43:47.291
Do you have pain relief patches?

770
00:43:47.374 --> 00:43:49.418
This counts as a workplace injury.

771
00:43:50.169 --> 00:43:54.340
Why do we keep spending money
when we're here to take it?

772
00:43:54.423 --> 00:43:56.634
Let's just leave. please.

773
00:43:56.717 --> 00:43:58.177
Just think of this as an investment.

774
00:44:03.015 --> 00:44:03.932
Boss!

775
00:44:05.142 --> 00:44:06.060
Boss!

776
00:44:30.834 --> 00:44:32.127
There's no movement. sir.

777
00:44:34.004 --> 00:44:36.006
Park Hae-kang isn't doing anything?

778
00:44:36.090 --> 00:44:36.924
No. sir.

779
00:44:37.966 --> 00:44:41.428
He's just walking
around the apartment complex

780
00:44:41.512 --> 00:44:42.763
and living quietly.

781
00:44:44.473 --> 00:44:46.600
He doesn't hate money.

782
00:44:47.309 --> 00:44:50.646
and he wouldn't just sit and watch
as his old boss dies.

783
00:44:53.357 --> 00:44:54.858
What's he up to?

784
00:44:55.484 --> 00:44:56.402
Mr. Kim.

785
00:44:57.069 --> 00:44:59.363
Did I overestimate Park Hae-kang?

786
00:45:00.572 --> 00:45:03.242
Should I keep watching him. sir?

787
00:45:06.370 --> 00:45:08.747
He'll have no choice but to come to me.

788
00:45:09.498 --> 00:45:12.960
That ledger will become useless
if Park Yong-man dies.

789
00:45:14.628 --> 00:45:15.462
You can go.

790
00:45:16.171 --> 00:45:17.005
Yes. sir.

791
00:45:38.527 --> 00:45:40.863
Even if you keep holding out
until the end.

792
00:45:42.531 --> 00:45:44.199
all that will be left

793
00:45:45.409 --> 00:45:47.828
is this single photo.

794
00:45:48.495 --> 00:45:49.872
You're such a fool.

795
00:45:50.873 --> 00:45:51.915
Park Hae-kang.

796
00:45:58.213 --> 00:46:00.382
I called for an urgent meeting today

797
00:46:01.049 --> 00:46:03.343
because something is happening
in True Value State

798
00:46:03.927 --> 00:46:06.638
that I simply cannot turn a blind eye to.

799
00:46:07.473 --> 00:46:08.640
President Jang.

800
00:46:08.724 --> 00:46:10.017
CONSTRUCTION DEFECTS

801
00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:11.268
What is that?

802
00:46:11.351 --> 00:46:12.561
What's that?

803
00:46:13.228 --> 00:46:14.605
Are those photos real?

804
00:46:14.688 --> 00:46:16.899
Is this why
the kindergarten was shut down?

805
00:46:16.982 --> 00:46:19.318
These are photos
from True Value's kindergarten.

806
00:46:19.401 --> 00:46:23.238
As you can see.
this goes beyond a minor defect.

807
00:46:23.864 --> 00:46:26.158
I had the kindergarten shut down
as the president.

808
00:46:26.241 --> 00:46:27.075
Hold on.

809
00:46:27.159 --> 00:46:29.995
Has the building really aged this fast?

810
00:46:30.078 --> 00:46:31.413
No.

811
00:46:31.497 --> 00:46:34.291
this is clearly a sign
of shoddy construction.

812
00:46:34.374 --> 00:46:36.210
-Shoddy construction?
-Shoddy construction?

813
00:46:38.795 --> 00:46:42.633
Do you know how serious an issue this is?

814
00:46:42.716 --> 00:46:45.135
This could make our property values
plummet overnight.

815
00:46:45.219 --> 00:46:46.428
That's not the problem!

816
00:46:46.512 --> 00:46:48.597
Don't you see the cracks in the photos?

817
00:46:49.306 --> 00:46:52.935
I trusted the director
and thought it was safe.

818
00:46:53.685 --> 00:46:57.064
The inspection company
stated that the kindergarten was safe

819
00:46:57.147 --> 00:47:00.901
because it was a subsidiary
of Taesan Construction.

820
00:47:05.155 --> 00:47:08.617
So they were putting our children
in danger the whole time?

821
00:47:09.868 --> 00:47:12.955
You're making a fuss
over something that hasn't happened yet.

822
00:47:13.038 --> 00:47:16.875
The president is being overly worried.
calling it shoddy construction.

823
00:47:16.959 --> 00:47:19.419
Let's not cause a commotion.

824
00:47:19.503 --> 00:47:21.505
This concerns the safety of our children.

825
00:47:21.588 --> 00:47:24.675
We must explain the situation
to the residents

826
00:47:24.758 --> 00:47:25.926
and make it public--

827
00:47:26.009 --> 00:47:27.219
Wait. Make it public?

828
00:47:27.302 --> 00:47:29.513
Can't we just get things repaired quietly?

829
00:47:29.596 --> 00:47:31.306
Repairs won't fix everything.

830
00:47:31.390 --> 00:47:34.643
We should file a complaint and demand
action from Taesan Construction.

831
00:47:34.726 --> 00:47:36.436
We can't send our kids back there.

832
00:47:37.062 --> 00:47:39.147
Then send them
to a different kindergarten.

833
00:47:39.231 --> 00:47:41.608
There are dozens of kindergartens
in our neighborhood.

834
00:47:41.692 --> 00:47:43.360
Right. Send them somewhere else.

835
00:47:43.443 --> 00:47:45.362
Imagine what will happen if rumors spread.

836
00:47:45.445 --> 00:47:47.489
Look. I got the chills
just thinking about it.

837
00:47:47.573 --> 00:47:49.032
I'm more scared about that.

838
00:47:49.116 --> 00:47:51.243
You should think
about the residents' assets.

839
00:47:51.326 --> 00:47:52.828
Their houses are everything to them.

840
00:47:52.911 --> 00:47:55.539
In any case.
this can never be made public.

841
00:47:56.707 --> 00:47:58.458
A president dropping apartment prices?

842
00:47:58.542 --> 00:47:59.918
Whose side are you even on?

843
00:48:00.419 --> 00:48:01.920
You should just step down!

844
00:48:02.004 --> 00:48:03.380
Yes. step down.

845
00:48:03.463 --> 00:48:04.464
Step down!

846
00:48:05.007 --> 00:48:07.134
Everyone. listen.

847
00:48:10.178 --> 00:48:13.682
You can't trade
our children's safety for money.

848
00:48:14.308 --> 00:48:16.852
And if an accident occurs
at the kindergarten.

849
00:48:16.935 --> 00:48:18.020
what would you do then?

850
00:48:18.103 --> 00:48:19.980
-You're just a tenant!
-You're just a tenant!

851
00:48:20.606 --> 00:48:22.065
The homeowners are speaking.

852
00:48:22.149 --> 00:48:24.026
You don't care
because it's not your own house.

853
00:48:24.109 --> 00:48:28.155
Property prices are a serious matter
directly tied to our livelihoods.

854
00:48:28.947 --> 00:48:30.449
Fine. I get it.

855
00:48:32.451 --> 00:48:34.119
Continue the meeting. President Park.

856
00:48:34.202 --> 00:48:35.037
Unbelievable.

857
00:48:41.752 --> 00:48:42.794
Just a moment.

858
00:48:45.047 --> 00:48:46.798
Who among you

859
00:48:46.882 --> 00:48:49.051
doesn't have any children?

860
00:48:49.134 --> 00:48:50.135
Raise your hands.

861
00:48:56.808 --> 00:48:57.809
All right. then.

862
00:48:58.352 --> 00:49:00.479
I will do my job as president.

863
00:49:00.562 --> 00:49:01.897
{\an8}PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

864
00:49:07.986 --> 00:49:08.820
Yes?

865
00:49:12.991 --> 00:49:14.284
What are you going to do?

866
00:49:16.703 --> 00:49:18.747
What will you do
about the defective construction?

867
00:49:18.830 --> 00:49:21.583
Are you going to drop it
just because they're opposing it?

868
00:49:21.667 --> 00:49:23.960
We should make a formal complaint…

869
00:49:24.044 --> 00:49:25.962
No. wait. Let's report this to the media.

870
00:49:26.546 --> 00:49:28.507
Lee Chung-won has control
over the media as well.

871
00:49:29.424 --> 00:49:31.551
So you're just going to sit back
and do nothing?

872
00:49:31.635 --> 00:49:34.596
If we can't use the media.
we can become the media instead.

873
00:49:42.688 --> 00:49:43.897
Ms. Kang is here too.

874
00:49:47.150 --> 00:49:48.276
Perfect timing. everyone.

875
00:49:48.360 --> 00:49:49.319
What?

876
00:49:51.780 --> 00:49:55.534
We came to tell you
we won't just transfer kindergartens.

877
00:49:55.617 --> 00:49:58.120
This isn't just
a minor construction mistake.

878
00:49:58.203 --> 00:50:00.497
They put our children's lives
at risk for money.

879
00:50:00.580 --> 00:50:02.457
We should ring the bell for society.

880
00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:04.376
You mean "sound the alarm."

881
00:50:04.960 --> 00:50:05.794
Right.

882
00:50:05.877 --> 00:50:08.422
Can you think of any ideas.
President Park?

883
00:50:15.637 --> 00:50:16.763
It's right here.

884
00:50:19.182 --> 00:50:20.016
Me?

885
00:50:21.977 --> 00:50:22.811
Why?

886
00:50:22.894 --> 00:50:24.312
DAMN IN-LAWS

887
00:50:27.691 --> 00:50:29.151
<i>Damn in-laws.</i>

888
00:50:29.234 --> 00:50:32.487
<i>Mother. only factories would make</i>

889
00:50:32.571 --> 00:50:35.198
<i>300 batches of kimchi.</i>

890
00:50:35.282 --> 00:50:36.950
<i>That's why I got…</i>

891
00:50:37.033 --> 00:50:38.535
You're shaking like crazy!

892
00:50:39.953 --> 00:50:42.122
You don't even have in-laws.
Why are you watching that?

893
00:50:42.205 --> 00:50:43.707
-Don't you know her?
-I don't.

894
00:50:43.790 --> 00:50:45.041
She's really popular.

895
00:50:45.125 --> 00:50:46.960
-Who is it?
-"Damn in-laws!"

896
00:50:48.253 --> 00:50:50.714
-She has over a million subscribers.
<i>-Damn in-laws!</i>

897
00:50:53.258 --> 00:50:54.885
That voice sounds familiar.

898
00:50:56.511 --> 00:50:57.721
"Damn in-laws"?

899
00:51:01.099 --> 00:51:04.227
Oh no. You caught me.

900
00:51:07.355 --> 00:51:09.941
This isn't going to be an exposé video.

901
00:51:10.025 --> 00:51:12.569
It's going to be a marketing video
for a luxury kindergarten.

902
00:51:12.652 --> 00:51:16.239
So keep the tone as luxurious
as you can. okay?

903
00:51:18.074 --> 00:51:20.702
Ms. Kang. begin when I give the sign.

904
00:51:21.620 --> 00:51:22.913
Don't worry.

905
00:51:22.996 --> 00:51:24.998
All right. Are you all ready?

906
00:51:31.588 --> 00:51:33.340
Let's go.

907
00:51:33.423 --> 00:51:34.466
Go on.

908
00:51:36.426 --> 00:51:39.429
Everyone. Taesan Construction
has introduced a special system

909
00:51:39.513 --> 00:51:41.473
to improve children's balance.

910
00:51:41.556 --> 00:51:44.643
An automatic floor-tilting system.

911
00:51:47.062 --> 00:51:49.356
When you place an apple on a table…

912
00:51:56.988 --> 00:51:59.950
As you can see.
they've installed this to help children

913
00:52:00.033 --> 00:52:01.201
build lower-body strength.

914
00:52:02.285 --> 00:52:04.871
Oh my. It seems like Taesan Construction

915
00:52:04.955 --> 00:52:07.457
wants to turn our kids
into future gymnastics champions.

916
00:52:10.377 --> 00:52:11.294
Oh. that's cold!

917
00:52:13.338 --> 00:52:16.091
You must be worried about
your children's skin in the dry winter.

918
00:52:16.174 --> 00:52:19.553
But here. there's a mist of cement dust
operating 24 hours a day.

919
00:52:19.636 --> 00:52:22.138
The damp atmosphere
gives off a high-end basement vibe.

920
00:52:22.222 --> 00:52:25.016
You could film <i>Parasite</i> here!

921
00:52:25.684 --> 00:52:26.601
How damp!

922
00:52:29.187 --> 00:52:32.816
Look at these luxurious drops of water
falling from the ceiling.

923
00:52:32.899 --> 00:52:35.151
Taesan Construction staff.

924
00:52:35.235 --> 00:52:38.154
would you like to come here
in person for a shower?

925
00:52:38.238 --> 00:52:39.072
Oh. that's cold!

926
00:52:39.155 --> 00:52:40.073
No way!

927
00:52:41.408 --> 00:52:42.909
And here's the highlight.

928
00:52:42.993 --> 00:52:46.246
Shall we see what they've hidden
behind this pretty facade

929
00:52:46.329 --> 00:52:49.082
{\an8}saying "Enrollment Open"?

930
00:52:49.165 --> 00:52:51.084
{\an8}Mothers. please reveal it!

931
00:52:55.338 --> 00:52:56.965
This is nuts.

932
00:52:58.341 --> 00:53:00.886
It seems they've made art
instead of a building.

933
00:53:00.969 --> 00:53:04.097
This premium crack pattern
is quite unique. isn't it?

934
00:53:04.848 --> 00:53:07.726
That's truly a magnificent crack.

935
00:53:07.809 --> 00:53:09.519
Subscribers.

936
00:53:09.603 --> 00:53:13.356
wouldn't it be a waste
to keep such a place to ourselves?

937
00:53:14.441 --> 00:53:17.527
So we'll share this secret with you all.

938
00:53:17.611 --> 00:53:19.362
Shoddy construction. zero conscience.

939
00:53:19.446 --> 00:53:20.614
The company name is…

940
00:53:21.531 --> 00:53:22.908
{\an8}-Tae.
-San.

941
00:53:22.991 --> 00:53:24.743
{\an8}-Con.
-Struction.

942
00:53:24.826 --> 00:53:25.785
No way!

943
00:53:26.828 --> 00:53:29.539
Damn in-laws.

944
00:53:29.623 --> 00:53:32.709
I might put up with in-laws.
but I won't put up with anyone

945
00:53:32.792 --> 00:53:34.210
harming our kids!

946
00:53:36.463 --> 00:53:38.131
{\an8}<i>Listen up. Taesan Construction.</i>

947
00:53:38.673 --> 00:53:41.593
{\an8}<i>We're getting back every penny</i>
<i>you skimmed from the rebar costs.</i>

948
00:53:41.676 --> 00:53:43.970
<i>so go ahead</i>
<i>and try holding out until the end.</i>

949
00:53:44.054 --> 00:53:46.222
Taesan Construction may silence the media.

950
00:53:46.306 --> 00:53:48.934
but they can't silence
my channel's subscribers.

951
00:53:49.017 --> 00:53:51.227
Should I upload the video now?

952
00:53:51.311 --> 00:53:52.812
Instead of fighting your in-laws.

953
00:53:52.896 --> 00:53:56.566
let's take on the construction company
for our children this time.

954
00:53:57.400 --> 00:53:58.902
All right. let's do this.

955
00:54:16.711 --> 00:54:18.505
{\an8}Boss. look at the view count going up.

956
00:54:18.588 --> 00:54:19.631
It's insane.

957
00:54:19.714 --> 00:54:23.718
Why didn't I know that Seo-jun's mom
was "Damn In-Laws"?

958
00:54:23.802 --> 00:54:25.136
I'm a subscriber.

959
00:54:25.220 --> 00:54:27.263
"Is their headquarters
built out of Styrofoam?"

960
00:54:27.347 --> 00:54:28.848
"Taesan loves shoddy construction."

961
00:54:28.932 --> 00:54:30.308
The comments are blowing up.

962
00:54:31.267 --> 00:54:34.062
They were fools
to mess with Korean mothers.

963
00:54:34.145 --> 00:54:37.232
They may silence the media.
but they can't silence the mothers.

964
00:54:37.315 --> 00:54:38.149
Right.

965
00:54:38.233 --> 00:54:40.360
Taesan Construction
should be responding soon.

966
00:54:40.944 --> 00:54:41.778
Of course.

967
00:54:42.779 --> 00:54:46.616
{\an8}We're contacting influencers
who are spreading the video

968
00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:48.159
and asking them to delete it.

969
00:54:48.743 --> 00:54:51.830
Most of them did
when we offered money. but…

970
00:54:51.913 --> 00:54:53.415
"But"?

971
00:54:54.582 --> 00:54:57.252
There are posts on
the True Value mothers' online community

972
00:54:57.335 --> 00:54:59.045
requesting an explanation from Taesan

973
00:54:59.129 --> 00:55:03.341
and a full safety inspection
of the apartment complex.

974
00:55:04.009 --> 00:55:06.594
What the hell is the legal team doing?

975
00:55:07.345 --> 00:55:10.473
Mothers' community or not.
just sue everyone.

976
00:55:10.557 --> 00:55:13.435
Make sure everyone who spreads the video

977
00:55:13.518 --> 00:55:16.354
will want to cut off their own hands.

978
00:55:16.938 --> 00:55:18.690
Yes. sir.

979
00:55:21.985 --> 00:55:23.778
SENIOR SECRETARY SONG U-SIK

980
00:55:24.446 --> 00:55:25.655
What about the old geezers?

981
00:55:29.367 --> 00:55:30.910
The Prosecutor General

982
00:55:30.994 --> 00:55:34.039
seems to be contacting
other construction company presidents.

983
00:55:35.415 --> 00:55:36.249
What?

984
00:55:37.125 --> 00:55:38.793
How dare he?

985
00:55:38.877 --> 00:55:42.505
It seems like he's trying to find
a company to keep Taesan in check.

986
00:55:43.089 --> 00:55:44.549
Keep Taesan in check?

987
00:55:46.926 --> 00:55:50.055
Who do they think they are
to keep me in check?

988
00:55:50.138 --> 00:55:54.017
{\an8}They're all just sitting around
waiting for me to bring them money.

989
00:55:56.269 --> 00:55:57.520
GONGYEONG DAILY LEE SANG-GYU

990
00:55:57.604 --> 00:55:59.939
These old geezers are all panicking.

991
00:56:00.732 --> 00:56:04.652
worried this will affect
the Oman New Town project.

992
00:56:05.695 --> 00:56:06.696
Park Hae-kang…

993
00:56:07.572 --> 00:56:08.865
Park Hae-kang!

994
00:56:10.992 --> 00:56:12.619
I loved his competence.

995
00:56:13.703 --> 00:56:15.288
but now that he's my enemy.

996
00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:17.457
I want to kill him.

997
00:56:21.169 --> 00:56:23.129
Not a single person is passing by.

998
00:56:23.213 --> 00:56:26.549
Why do we have to sit out here
in the freezing cold?

999
00:56:26.633 --> 00:56:29.761
The boss told us to make sure
nobody goes inside.

1000
00:56:29.844 --> 00:56:32.097
They'll come to get rid of the evidence.

1001
00:56:32.180 --> 00:56:34.140
I put up thermal sensors
all around the entrance.

1002
00:56:34.224 --> 00:56:36.059
The alarm will go off
even if an ant walks by.

1003
00:56:36.142 --> 00:56:38.603
But don't the Taesan guys sleep at all?

1004
00:56:38.686 --> 00:56:41.606
They'd have to be paid
for night shifts too.

1005
00:56:41.689 --> 00:56:42.732
Don't be stupid.

1006
00:56:42.816 --> 00:56:45.527
Would thieves even care about labor laws?

1007
00:56:45.610 --> 00:56:46.736
Geez.

1008
00:56:47.403 --> 00:56:48.696
Intruder alert!

1009
00:56:49.322 --> 00:56:50.657
Cover me!

1010
00:57:02.085 --> 00:57:02.919
Damn it.

1011
00:57:03.461 --> 00:57:06.047
Is this a secret weapon sent by Taesan?

1012
00:57:06.131 --> 00:57:07.882
Sorry. that's the snack I was eating.

1013
00:57:08.675 --> 00:57:10.635
Just pick one. Doze off or eat.

1014
00:57:10.718 --> 00:57:11.970
Intruder alert canceled.

1015
00:57:13.221 --> 00:57:15.431
Good job. Stick to the manual.

1016
00:57:15.515 --> 00:57:16.808
Manual. my foot…

1017
00:57:31.364 --> 00:57:32.824
This is so satisfying.

1018
00:57:32.907 --> 00:57:35.660
We need to have <i>japchae</i> to celebrate.

1019
00:57:35.743 --> 00:57:36.661
Boss. look at this.

1020
00:57:36.744 --> 00:57:39.164
Our community forum
is blowing up right now.

1021
00:57:39.247 --> 00:57:41.291
Lee Chung-won's going
to feel pressured for sure.

1022
00:57:41.374 --> 00:57:42.542
Right.

1023
00:57:43.877 --> 00:57:46.004
He still pisses me off. though.
How dare he?

1024
00:57:46.087 --> 00:57:48.840
If he lays a finger on our old boss.

1025
00:57:48.923 --> 00:57:51.885
I'm going to tear
the whole Oman New Town apart.

1026
00:57:53.219 --> 00:57:55.263
You shouldn't slice the carrots like that!

1027
00:57:55.346 --> 00:57:56.556
This is for the <i>japchae</i>.

1028
00:57:56.639 --> 00:57:58.391
The sizes are all different.

1029
00:57:58.475 --> 00:57:59.767
Is this for Gyeong-buk?

1030
00:57:59.851 --> 00:58:01.978
Why are you cutting them
into whale shapes?

1031
00:58:02.061 --> 00:58:05.190
Je-gil. you should be helping me out here.

1032
00:58:05.273 --> 00:58:06.733
You're just staring at that forum.

1033
00:58:06.816 --> 00:58:09.068
I should just destroy that laptop.

1034
00:58:09.152 --> 00:58:11.321
-Look at him.
-Wait. Boss.

1035
00:58:11.404 --> 00:58:13.198
I think you should see this.

1036
00:58:14.991 --> 00:58:16.242
Mr. Park.

1037
00:58:16.326 --> 00:58:18.578
That post on the forum…

1038
00:58:18.661 --> 00:58:20.413
What's going on?

1039
00:58:22.749 --> 00:58:24.584
EXPOSING PARK HAE-KANG'S CORRUPTION

1040
00:58:30.381 --> 00:58:32.926
I'm the facility manager
of True Value State.

1041
00:58:34.093 --> 00:58:35.803
Choi Yeong-jae.

1042
00:58:36.387 --> 00:58:37.305
<i>Today.</i>

1043
00:58:38.598 --> 00:58:41.184
<i>I am staking</i>
<i>my lifelong professional integrity</i>

1044
00:58:41.809 --> 00:58:43.603
<i>on the truth I'm about to reveal.</i>

1045
00:58:44.604 --> 00:58:47.524
The 17.8 billion won
in the long-term repair reserve fund

1046
00:58:47.607 --> 00:58:50.151
{\an8}that all the residents
gathered over the past years…

1047
00:58:52.570 --> 00:58:54.322
was embezzled by President Park Hae-kang

1048
00:58:56.366 --> 00:58:58.826
and the accounting manager. Kang Ha-jeong.

1049
00:59:00.119 --> 00:59:01.162
as part

1050
00:59:02.622 --> 00:59:03.831
of an organized scheme.

1051
00:59:04.624 --> 00:59:06.543
<i>I am ashamed to admit</i>

1052
00:59:07.168 --> 00:59:10.088
<i>that as the facility manager.</i>
<i>I was deceived and used by them.</i>

1053
00:59:10.171 --> 00:59:11.798
<i>blinded by their elaborate collusion</i>

1054
00:59:12.632 --> 00:59:13.925
<i>and falsified documents.</i>

1055
00:59:14.008 --> 00:59:17.136
What kind of bullshit is this?

1056
00:59:18.179 --> 00:59:20.014
<i>It's late.</i>
<i>but I found the courage to confess</i>

1057
00:59:20.598 --> 00:59:22.600
<i>in order to prevent any further harm.</i>

1058
00:59:22.684 --> 00:59:24.811
<i>President Park embezzled the reserve fund.</i>

1059
00:59:25.853 --> 00:59:27.063
Goodness.

1060
00:59:27.146 --> 00:59:28.856
What? Embezzled?

1061
00:59:28.940 --> 00:59:29.983
Oh my goodness.

1062
00:59:30.066 --> 00:59:31.609
<i>They embezzled how much?</i>

1063
00:59:31.693 --> 00:59:33.611
<i>It's 17.8 billion won!</i>

1064
00:59:34.571 --> 00:59:36.364
No way! 17.8 billion?

1065
00:59:38.199 --> 00:59:39.826
They embezzled 17.8 billion?

1066
00:59:40.743 --> 00:59:43.871
This doesn't even compare
to President Seo.

1067
00:59:44.747 --> 00:59:46.374
<i>I promise to cooperate</i>

1068
00:59:47.875 --> 00:59:49.794
<i>with any investigations.</i>

1069
00:59:50.503 --> 00:59:51.879
You still can't reach Mr. Choi?

1070
00:59:51.963 --> 00:59:52.964
<i>The number you've dialed…</i>

1071
00:59:53.047 --> 00:59:55.133
His phone's turned off.

1072
00:59:55.216 --> 00:59:57.093
Should we just unplug all the phones?

1073
00:59:57.176 --> 00:59:58.678
<i>Lastly.</i>

1074
00:59:58.761 --> 01:00:02.181
<i>I sincerely apologize to all the residents</i>

1075
01:00:03.558 --> 01:00:04.851
<i>of True Value.</i>

1076
01:00:16.154 --> 01:00:17.864
I can't believe this.

1077
01:00:17.947 --> 01:00:20.950
He's claiming that Mr. Park
and Ha-jeong took the 17.8 billion?

1078
01:00:21.034 --> 01:00:22.952
Why is this happening?

1079
01:00:23.036 --> 01:00:24.078
This is ridiculous.

1080
01:00:24.162 --> 01:00:25.788
Mr. Choi is stabbing us in the back

1081
01:00:25.872 --> 01:00:27.498
when he's the one who took the money.

1082
01:00:28.249 --> 01:00:29.208
Boss.

1083
01:00:30.293 --> 01:00:31.127
What do we do?

1084
01:00:31.878 --> 01:00:33.963
-Boss!
-What should we do?

1085
01:00:34.589 --> 01:00:35.632
Who is it this time?

1086
01:00:35.715 --> 01:00:36.883
Tell them to come back later.

1087
01:00:38.051 --> 01:00:39.636
<i>Police! Open the door.</i>

1088
01:00:41.387 --> 01:00:42.347
-Pol…
-Police?

1089
01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:43.723
How did they come so quickly?

1090
01:00:43.806 --> 01:00:45.892
I'll go and buy some time.

1091
01:00:45.975 --> 01:00:47.602
-No. wait!
-Why?

1092
01:00:47.685 --> 01:00:49.896
Don't open the door just yet.

1093
01:00:50.647 --> 01:00:52.982
What do we do now. Mr. Park?

1094
01:00:53.650 --> 01:00:55.568
Lizard. Ha-jeong. get inside.

1095
01:00:57.236 --> 01:00:58.404
You guys hide too.

1096
01:00:58.488 --> 01:00:59.947
-Ms. Kang. come on.
-Hurry up!

1097
01:01:00.031 --> 01:01:01.491
What are we supposed to do?

1098
01:01:01.991 --> 01:01:03.618
-Hurry up.
-Go inside.

1099
01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:16.798
Sangwon Police Major Crimes Unit.
Mr. Park Hae-kang?

1100
01:01:17.382 --> 01:01:19.258
You're under arrest

1101
01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:20.968
for embezzlement and breach of trust.

1102
01:01:21.052 --> 01:01:24.681
Due to the risk of flight.
we're arresting you without a warrant.

1103
01:01:24.764 --> 01:01:27.100
You have the right to retain an attorney.

1104
01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.602
to present your defense.
and to remain silent.

1105
01:01:29.686 --> 01:01:31.979
Anything you say can
and will be used against you--

1106
01:01:32.063 --> 01:01:32.939
Let's go.

1107
01:01:34.649 --> 01:01:35.483
Boss!

1108
01:01:35.566 --> 01:01:37.402
Let go!

1109
01:01:37.485 --> 01:01:39.070
-Don't touch the officer.
-Step back!

1110
01:01:39.153 --> 01:01:40.738
-Hey.
-Wait!

1111
01:01:42.156 --> 01:01:43.950
You should explain what's going on!

1112
01:01:44.033 --> 01:01:44.867
Boss.

1113
01:01:44.951 --> 01:01:46.703
The facility manager was lying!

1114
01:01:46.786 --> 01:01:48.454
-Boss.
-Boss.

1115
01:01:49.038 --> 01:01:49.997
Mr. Park.

1116
01:02:02.927 --> 01:02:05.346
THE APARTMENT JOB

1117
01:02:29.454 --> 01:02:32.874
{\an8}How can this be the face of someone
who took 17.8 billion won?

1118
01:02:32.957 --> 01:02:34.333
{\an8}Let me talk to you. Mr. Choi.

1119
01:02:34.417 --> 01:02:35.710
{\an8}What's with you?

1120
01:02:37.378 --> 01:02:38.796
{\an8}Get him!

1121
01:02:38.880 --> 01:02:41.632
{\an8}<i>I'm actually curious.</i>

1122
01:02:41.716 --> 01:02:42.925
{\an8}<i>Did you really think</i>

1123
01:02:43.009 --> 01:02:46.095
{\an8}<i>exposing that shoddy construction</i>
<i>would achieve some great justice?</i>

1124
01:02:46.763 --> 01:02:48.097
{\an8}Your photos look great.

1125
01:02:48.181 --> 01:02:50.099
{\an8}<i>We should be sticking together.</i>

1126
01:02:50.183 --> 01:02:52.143
{\an8}<i>Stick together and do what?</i>

1127
01:02:52.226 --> 01:02:54.061
{\an8}<i>We have to stay right here. as a family.</i>

1128
01:02:54.145 --> 01:02:55.396
{\an8}You thief!

1129
01:02:56.272 --> 01:02:57.356
{\an8}I won't run away

1130
01:02:57.440 --> 01:03:00.234
{\an8}<i>until we catch the one</i>
<i>who took the 17.8 billion.</i>

1131
01:03:00.318 --> 01:03:01.569
{\an8}It was my oversight.

1132
01:03:01.652 --> 01:03:04.238
{\an8}<i>We will rebuild it</i>
<i>into one of the finest kindergartens.</i>

1133
01:03:04.322 --> 01:03:05.364
{\an8}<i>President Lee Chung-won.</i>

1134
01:03:05.448 --> 01:03:08.451
{\an8}<i>Are you going to demolish all 9.800</i>
<i>apartments here and rebuild them again?</i>

1135
01:03:08.534 --> 01:03:11.162
{\an8}<i>He's really blowing everything up.</i>

1136
01:03:14.749 --> 01:03:16.751
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
